// Date: 2026-11-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.007
// Description: Detects the execution of EvilClippy. A dual use tool that assists in hiding malicious VBA macro
//   code inside MS Office documents. Attackers can use it to stomp the VBA source code of a macro
//   enabled document while keeping the compiled p-code, in order to evade static analysis tools.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/outflanknl/EvilClippy
//   - https://www.outflank.nl/blog/2019/05/05/evil-clippy-ms-office-maldoc-assistant/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/192637bd45d53e584c3f8c6d3be83b9cf90d90fa/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_evilclippy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\EvilClippy.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "EvilClippy.exe"
